      {
        "step": 42,
        "message": "The local-correlation refinement is converging without large changes to the already stable lower landmarks. I\u2019m keeping multiple candidate fits for the upper points rather than trusting a single optimizer minimum; the final selection will be based on the actual 3D branch geometry."
      },
      {
        "step": 68,
        "message": "The denser fit resolves the two ambiguous landmarks: q02 aligns with the same small side branch on the peripheral vessel, and q04 aligns with the vessel/diaphragm contour rather than a nearby look-alike. I\u2019m doing one edge-based consistency check now; the remaining points agree across fits to within a few millimetres."
      }
    ],
    "3d": [
      {
        "step": 11,
        "message": "The query points are concentrated on pulmonary vessel bifurcations and pleural/mediastinal boundaries, so they should provide strong local 3D intensity cues. I\u2019m estimating the respiratory deformation in the source-to-target direction and will compare several registration settings to detect unstable matches."
      },
      {
        "step": 22,
        "message": "The global deformable fields disagree at several peripheral vessels, while direct 3D patch matching produces a much clearer and anatomically consistent correspondence (especially for q02, q04, and q08). I\u2019m now refining those local matches continuously and allowing a small local affine change so lung expansion does not bias the landmark centers."
      },
      {
        "step": 35,
        "message": "The vessel-level matches are stable to roughly 1\u20132 mm for seven points. One mediastinal point (q06) has two nearby solutions along the same boundary; I\u2019m using a smoother neighborhood-based registration as an independent check before finalizing it."
      },
      {
        "step": 45,
        "message": "The independent local rigid/similarity fits confirm the vessel matches and resolve q06 at the lower of the two boundary candidates. The final correspondences are mutually consistent with nearby vessel motion; I\u2019m writing the ordered world-coordinate result and running schema/finite/bounds checks."
      }
